  "gaps": [
    "The concentration is recorded as one 18-semester-hour block because the student's choice is unknown. The Digital Communication and Media Design option is COMM356, COMM365, COMM375, COMM385, COMM415 and COMM456, at 3 each. The Strategic Communication option is COMM351, COMM361, COMM370, COMM380, COMM410 and COMM450, at 3 each.",
    "The Communication 'Select 1 course from the following' list shows only ENGL220. The capture may have dropped other options.",
    "The capture states no residency rule or minimum number of credits that must be completed at the institution.",
    "The capture states no transfer-credit limits.",
    "COMM211 and COMM240 appear in both the Civics, Political & Social Sciences gen-ed list and the Major Required list. The capture does not say whether one course may count toward both. Electives must be 'courses that have not been used to fulfill requirements listed above.'",
    "The capture states no minimum grade, GPA, or upper-division credit requirements.",
    "Footnote 1 on Arts & Humanities: literature courses require ENGL101 or ENGL110. The COMM498 prerequisite is 'Senior Standing and completion of all major courses prior to enrollment.'"
  ],
